<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03WS">Definition <span data-tag="03WS">8.4.8.1</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a locally small $\infty $-category which admits small colimits. We say that an object $X \in \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is <em>atomic</em> if the corepresentable functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ h^{X}: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}\quad \quad Y \mapsto \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}(X,Y) \]
</div>
<p> preserves small colimits. </p>
